      "text": [
        " أَوْلَمَ إِسْمَاعِيلُ فَقَالَ لَهُ أَبُو عَبْدِ اللَّهِ ( عليه السلام ) عَلَيْكَ بِالْمَسَاكِينِ فَأَشْبِعْهُمْ فَإِنَّ اللَّهَ عَزَّ وَ جَلَّ يَقُولُ وَ ما يُبْدِئُ الْباطِلُ وَ ما يُعِيدُ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Ali Bin Ibrahim, from his father, from Ibn Abu Umeyr, from Hammad Bin Usman who said, ",
          "‘Ismail had a banquet, so Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> said to him: ‘It is upon you with (inviting) the poor, so satiate them, for Allah<sup>azwj</sup> Mighty and Majestic is Saying <span class=\"ibTxt\"><a href=\"/#/books/quran:34#h49\"><a href=\"/books/quran:34#h49\">[34:49]</a></a> and what the falsehood started, shall not return</span>’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "16. Ali ibn Ibrahim has narrated from his father from ibn abu ‘Umayr from Hammad ibn ‘Uthaman who has said the following: “’Isma’il prepared food for a ceremony and abu ‘ Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, said to him, ’You must pay attention to the destitute to satisfy their hunger. Allah, most Majestic, most Glorious, says, “Falsehood is not served first or revisited for service.” <a href=\"/#/books/quran:34#h49\"><a href=\"/books/quran:34#h49\">[34:49]</a></a>”’ "
        ]
      }
    },
